variantes.contenu_markdown:
Food can be contaminated in many ways. Give a different one each time:
1. by food handlers with dirty hands, or by coughing and sneezing;
2. by flies, cockroaches and rats landing on food;
3. by dirty utensils, cloths and worktops;
4. by raw food touching cooked food (cross-contamination);
5. by dirty water used to wash or cook food;
6. by soil on unwashed vegetables and fruits;
7. by dust and refuse;
8. by chemicals such as insecticides and cleaning liquids;
9. by poor storage, such as leaving food uncovered or warm.
